  "id": "cognitive-interdependence",
  "term": "cognitive interdependence",
  "definition": "Cognitive interdependence is the degree to which a person mentally includes their romantic relationship in their sense of self. It reflects seeing oneself and one’s partner as a shared, collective “we” rather than as fully separate individuals.",
